/fig><fig id="f13-mder-4-197" position="float"><label>Figure 13</label><caption><p>Tip position for bottom control knob (up-down movement).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="mder-4-197f13"/></fig><fig id="f14-mder-4-197" position="float"><label>Figure 14</label><caption><p>Colonoscopy training model with porcine colon. Air is inserted to open the lumen for more realistic intubation.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="mder-4-197f14"/></fig><fig id="f15-mder-4-197" position="float"><label>Figure 15</label><caption><p>Snapshots of the porcine colon for the various parts during intubation.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="mder-4-197f15"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-mder-4-197" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Range of rotational speeds for bottom knob</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Initial rotation (deg)</th><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x003c9;</italic> (deg/s)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0&#x02013;30</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">99.3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30&#x02013;60</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">96.9</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">60&#x02013;90</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">95.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">90&#x02013;120</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">94.1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">120&#x02013;150</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">91.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">150&#x02013;180</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">92.0</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-group></article>